{"/api/discogs/artist/1007010/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1007010","image":"https://i.discogs.com/JnyVDVFUNtfOY0heeU3Q_y9MUKe7soKWuSP9MUQXe-A/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:549/w:588/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEwMDcw/MTAtMTY5MTE4MTU0/NC05MzM3LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/utXVKtqzq3MhJ0BSQ3QXUBNzYtwSx0ije5ocRjKs-Vw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEwMDcw/MTAtMTY5MTE4MTU0/NC05MzM3LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"American jazz-rock, soft rock and blue-eyed soul band formed in 1980 by keyboardist and singer Neil Larsen and guitarist and singer Buzz Feiten.\n\nBoth musicians had previously played together in the band Full Moon during the early 1970s and worked as session musicians for numerous artists, including Rickie Lee Jones.\n\nSigned to Warner Bros. Records, the group released their self-titled debut album in 1980, produced by Tommy LiPuma. Their single \"Who'll Be the Fool Tonight\" reached No. 29 on the US Billboard Hot 100.\n\nTheir second album, \"Full Moon\", was released in 1982. Other musicians associated with the band included Willie Weeks (bass), Art Rodriguez (drums) and Lenny Castro (percussion).","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:1007010","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":981378,"name":"Full Moon (5)"}],"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":227790,"name":"Neil Larsen"},{"active":true,"id":252196,"name":"Lenny Castro"},{"active":true,"id":256149,"name":"Willie Weeks"},{"active":true,"id":320003,"name":"Buzzy Feiten"},{"active":true,"id":565365,"name":"Art Rodriguez"}],"namevariations":["Larsen Feiten Band","Larsen-Feiton Band"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/1007010-Larsen-Feiten-Band","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.bluedesert.dk/larsenfeiten.html","http://www.myspace.com/larsonfeitenband"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/1105110/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1105110","image":"https://i.discogs.com/k5WD6uGqpFMvkQCzw7KOebUmlw7fCwwvRVzSe