50/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTY1Ny0x/MjczMTIxMzMwLmpw/ZWc.jpeg","profile":"[a=Richard D. James] ([a=Aphex Twin]) and [a=Mike Paradinas] (leader of the [l=Planet Mu] label who is better known as [a=µ-ziq]) joined forces in 1994 to form a project called Mike & Rich. The duo released one album titled \"Expert Knob Twiddlers\".","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:657","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":383,"name":"Mike Paradinas"},{"active":true,"id":435132,"name":"Richard D. James"}],"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/657-Mike-Rich","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.myspace.com/expertknobtwiddlers","https://mikeandrich.bandcamp.com/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/71872/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"71872","image":"https://i.discogs.com/mPGS1AXW-J3EwVOmj6-yQr8l_P-LB1Vl-gRCBK4q_No/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:596/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTcxODcy/LTE3MTU1NjU0MzMt/ODQwOS5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/96uMXPWuduMTwoHgb5RVeb7mLUk9stM0ibGauxuNChY/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTcxODcy/LTE3MTU1NjU0MzMt/ODQwOS5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"American singer songwriter, active from the 2nd half of the 1960s until his death aged 28. Born: 14 February 1947, Washington, D.C., USA. Died: 29 June 1975. Santa Monica. CA. USA.\n\nBuckley started out as a folk singer but quickly stood out for his extraordinary voice and compositions. He further built his reputation with forays into experimental music and improvisation, which can be heard on the albums Happy Sad, Lorca and Starsailor. Those albums never brought him commercial success, and in the third phase of his career Buckley went for a more commercial sound - again with little success at the time.\n\nBuckley died as the result of a lethal cocktail of celebratory binge-drinking and a heroin overdose at the age of 28, the day after completing the last show of a USA tour in Dallas, Texas.\n\nOn October 25, 1965, he married [a=Mary Guibert]. When she became pregnant, Tim abandoned her and eventually they divorced in October 1966, about a month before their son, [a=Jeff Buckley], was born.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:71872","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":[{"active":true,"id":2261146,"name":"The Bohemians (2)"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["Buckely","Buckley","T. Buckley","T.Buckley","Tim Backley","Tim Bucley","Timothy Buckley","Timothy Charles Buckley III"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/71872-Tim-Buckley","type":"artist","urls":["http://timbuckleymusic.com/","http://timbuckley.net/","https://timbuckley.bandcamp.com/","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tim_Buckley","http://www.whosampled.com/Tim-Buckley/","https://www.leeunderwood.net/Interviews/05_starsailor.html","https://www.rockzirkus.de/blog/2022/01/tim-buckley-jeff-buckley-tragische-rocker-11/","https://www.allmusic.com/artist/tim-buckley-mn0000595101","https://www.music-info-net.com/pro/tragik-rock/3418202_tragik-rock-timothy-charles-buckley-iii-tim-buckley-us-dc"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/8299/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"8299","image":"https://i.discogs.com/0hQmhj9VT8bfVXZ5T8YR3XeklYyo8H4AROO2A2Uz1SU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTgyOTkt/MTcwNzY3Njc5NC05/MzQ5LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/0QSeQVqJAcTn1uoQdJ1hy3benMnm4t8TSCpj3dMPGpw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTgyOTkt/MTcwNzY3Njc5NC05/MzQ5LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Icelandic post-rock band from Reykjavík. Known for their ethereal sound, frontman Jónsi's falsetto vocals, and the use of bowed guitar, the band's music is also noticeable for its incorporation of classical and minimalist aesthetic elements. The name \"Sigur Rós\" is Icelandic for \"Victory Rose\". The band is named after Jónsi's newborn sister [a=Sigurrós Elín Birgisdóttir]. \r\nJón Þór \"Jónsi\" Birgisson (guitar and vocals), Georg Holm (bass) and Ágúst Ævar Gunnarsson (drums) formed the group in Reykjavík in January 1994. Ágúst Ævar Gunnarsson retired after the release of the second album to be replaced by Orri Páll Dýrason. The band was joined by Kjartan Sveinsson on keyboards in 1998. Kjartan Sveinsson left the band in 2013. Orri Páll Dýrason left the band in 2018 facing allegations of sexual assult writing “I cannot have these serious allegations influence the band and the important and beautiful work that has been done there for the last years.”\r\nThe band announced Kjartan Sveinsson's return to the band in February 2022.\r\nLine-up (As of Nov. 2022): Jón Þór Birgisson (guitar, vocals), Georg Holm (bass guitar), Kjartan Sveinsson (keyboards), Ólafur Björn Ólafsson (drums, brass, organ)\r\n\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:8299","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":false,"id":355602,"name":"Orri Páll Dýrason"},{"active":true,"id":355603,"name":"Kjartan Sveinsson"},{"active":true,"id":428286,"name":"Georg Hólm"},{"active":false,"id":509724,"name":"Ágúst Ævar Gunnarsson"},{"active":true,"id":669806,"name":"Jón Þór Birgisson"}],"namevariations":["Cigar Ros","Cigar Rós","Sigu Rós","Sigur Ros","Sigur Ross","Sigur Ròs","Sigur Rós (Triple Nipple)","Sigurós","Victory Rose","シガー・ロス","席格若斯樂團"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/8299-Sigur-Rós","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.sigurros.com","https://www.facebook.com/sigurros","https://www.instagram.com/sigurros/","https://twitter.com/sigurros","https://www.youtube.com/user/sigurros","https://sigurros.bandcamp.com/","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigur_R%C3%B3s","http://www.popplagid.com/sigur_ros.htm","https://www.imdb.com/name/nm1460176/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/921864/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"921864","image":"https://i.discogs.com/mgIwqonpOy1RBSfhNteoTwJERHOexmbNC_W_lf1x_-g/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:475/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTkyMTg2/NC0xNTg3OTA0MDA4/LTU2MTguanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/Dh8TTCOyv7rrzrzhbq27SwgRXgTgeI-hj6AHqu8SnPA/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTkyMTg2/NC0xNTg3OTA0MDA4/LTU2MTguanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Johnny Reed McKinzie, Jr., (born March 31, 1985), better known by his stage name Jay Rock, is an American rapper, singer, songwriter and record producer from Watts, California. Rock ultimately chose to pursue a career as a rapper over a life of street crime, after Anthony Tiffith, the founder and CEO of the independent record label Top Dawg Entertainment (TDE), found Rock in 2005 and signed him to his label. In 2007, alongside TDE, Rock secured a recording contract with Warner Bros. Records and later Asylum Records, but after both mergers fell through, the label signed with Strange Music, after Tech N9ne, Missouri-based rapper and founder of the label, met with them and offered Rock a record deal.\r\n\r\nSince 2006, Rock has released several mixtapes and is perhaps best known for his 2008 commercial debut single, \"All My Life (In the Ghetto)\", which features fellow American rappers Lil Wayne and will.i.am. Apart from his solo career, Rock is also known for being a member of the hip hop supergroup Black Hippy, alongside fellow West Coast rappers and TDE label-mates Kendrick Lamar, Schoolboy Q and Ab-Soul. In 2011, after signing his joint-venture deal with Strange Music, Rock's often-delayed and long-awaited debut studio album, Follow Me Home, was released in July of that year. The album was supported by the singles \"All My Life (In the Ghetto)\" and \"Hood Gone Love It\". His second studio album 90059 was released in September 2015. It was supported by the singles \"Money Trees Deuce\", \"Gumbo\" and the title track. In June 2018, Rock released his third studio album ‘’Redemption’’. All three albums have achieved relative critical and commercial success.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:921864","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":1245726,"name":"Johnny McKinzie"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["J Rocc","J Rock","J-Rock","JAYROCK","Jay Rocc","Jay Rok","Jay-Rock","Jayrock"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/921864-Jay-Rock-2","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.facebook.com/jayrock","http://twitter.com/jayrock","http://www.jayrockmusic.com/","","http://equipboard.com/pros/jay-rock"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/987660/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"987660","image":"https://i.discogs.com/5lBvnMi54SQ3jJ_DsWDuSABw2rOyCMJ4jY4YKkZV_zI/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTk4NzY2/MC0xNjI0Mjc2MTg0/LTIyOTEuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/OabK75dqkd9QdrMxuwtlgiljp_0YtAxiguCdj3XlXgs/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTk4NzY2/MC0xNjI0Mjc2MTg0/LTIyOTEuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Based in Tokyo, and having lived in London for 5 years, Anchorsong - aka [a=Masaaki Yoshida] - is a producer and solo live act. He has become globally recognised for his unique live shows, as he creates electronic music completely live using a sampler (MPC2500) and a keyboard. While he mainly performs solo, he frequently augments this setup with a string quartet.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:987660","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":2909917,"name":"Masaaki Yoshida"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/987660-Anchorsong","type":"artist","urls":["http://anchorsong.com/","https://soundcloud.com/anchorsong","https://www.facebook.com/Anchorsong","https://twitter.com/Anchorsong","https://anchorsong.bandcamp.com/","https://www.youtube.com/user/yohage","https://www.songkick.com/artists/1965693-anchorsong","https://myspace.com/anchorsong","http://www.tru-thoughts.co.uk/artists/anchorsong","http://anchorsong.jugem.jp/"]}},"/api/discogs/label/1120990/profile":{"cache